# Information units, from IEC 80000-13:2008: the bit and the byte (8 bit), with decimal and binary prefixes.
# Not SI units: the bit is an alternate dimensionless atom, as the radian is in si.units.
# Format: symbol:name formula [Type]; '~' defines an alternate unit; '#' starts a comment.

@system Information

bit:bit ~
B:byte 8 bit

# Kilo and up only: other metric prefixes do not apply to these units (no dB).
@prefixed bit k M G T Ki Mi Gi Ti
@prefixed B k M G T P E Ki Mi Gi Ti Pi Ei
